# Normalize line endings.
#
# The working copy on Windows/OneDrive is CRLF while every commit in this
# repo's history stores LF. With no .gitattributes and core.autocrlf unset,
# git treated that as a real change: `git diff` reported all 28 tracked files
# fully rewritten (~6,800 lines), which buries the two-line fix you actually
# made and makes review or `git blame` useless.
#
# text=auto eol=lf  ->  LF in the repository and in the working tree.
# Windows editors (VS Code, PyCharm, Notepad) all handle LF fine.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary — never touch these.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.parquet binary
*.xlsx binary
